{"key": "47e355eea09f172de0d69690b04474d1", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "Here are the steps from the sources for a terminal with no connection. They cover the chip and the connection tests.\n\n1. Turn the terminal off, then open the back cover. Put the chip in the slot marked SIM1 or SIM2, with the metal part facing down. [1]\n2. Close the cover and turn the terminal on. Wait for the data network to connect. When it shows a connected network (2G or 3G), the terminal is ready to use. [1]\n3. Run a communication test to check that the chip is connected. [1]\n4. If you get error ADQ 1-84, which is a signal fluctuation, press the Function key and enter 25. Enter the Operator Password, then select Function 46. Make a test sale. [5]\n5. If you get error ADQ 1-87, which is a chip registration error, first confirm the chip is properly inserted. Press Function, enter 25, then enter the Merchant Password. Select Function 46, then Function 90. Make a test sale. [3]\n\nI can propose opening a support ticket for terminal T1988B with the reason \"no connection\". Nothing runs until you confirm, and the proposal expires after 15 minutes [policy:capabilities]. I haven't opened a ticket yet.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CgkbRDw1kubn3guXZAQaq", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2862}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2862, "cache_read_input_tokens": 3126, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 393, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "role": "agent", "scope": "approval-04#0"}
{"key": "af5887ef6c71ea4489a35b739842699d", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "I've proposed a support ticket for terminal T1988B with the reason \"no connection\". It's waiting for your confirmation, and nothing has been opened yet. The action ID is A-3922ff0f. Per [policy:capabilities], the proposal expires after 15 minutes. Do you confirm?\n\nThe terminal data shows T1988B offline with no signal on the chip connection. It has been offline for 5 hours, and its last contact was 05/11/2026 at 14:46.\n\nWhile you decide, these steps from the manual may help:\n1. Turn the terminal off and open the back cover. Put the chip in the SIM1 or SIM2 slot with the metal part facing down. [sup-duvidas-05]\n2. Close the cover and turn it on. Wait for the data network to connect (2G or 3G). [sup-duvidas-05]\n3. Run a communication test to check the chip is connected. [sup-duvidas-05]\n4. Error ADQ 1-84 (signal fluctuation): press Function and enter 25. Enter the Operator Password, select Function 46, then make a test sale. [sup-erro-adq-1-84-01]\n5. Error ADQ 1-87 (chip registration): confirm the chip is inserted. Press Function, enter 25, then enter the Merchant Password. Select Function 46, then Function 90, then make a test sale. [sup-erro-adq-1-87-01]", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CgkbRUrCG4mPEY2K3U3LR", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 804}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 804, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4051, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 460, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "role": "supervisor", "scope": "approval-04#0"}
